3. Modified Versions

If You make a Material Modification to the Software, You must clearly
indicate that changes were made. Modified Versions must not be presented
as the original Software.

Specifically:

(a) You shall include a prominent notice in all copies of the Modified
Version stating that the Software has been modified from its original
version, including the name of the modifying party and the year of
modification. This notice shall be placed in a file such as "NOTICE" or
"MODIFICATIONS" included with the distribution, or in documentation
accompanying the distribution. Notices required under this Section may be
combined into a single notice listing all modifying parties, provided the
notice clearly identifies that the Software has been modified from its
original version and is not the original Software.

(b) If You Distribute Publicly a Modified Version, You must either:

(i) use a Project Name different from the Project Name of the version You
modified, or

(ii) prominently display a notice in all user-facing documentation and,
where such notices are technically feasible given the nature of the
Software, in the Software's user interface or, if the Software has no user
interface, in its startup output or version text, stating that the version
is modified and is not the original Software.

The notice required by this subsection may be the same notice as that
required by subsection (a).

For purposes of this subsection, a Project Name that includes the Project
Name of the version You modified, or a name confusingly similar to it,
does not satisfy the requirement of a different Project Name.

For purposes of this subsection, "user-facing documentation" means the
primary documentation distributed with the Software, such as a README,
manual, or help text.

